# pathiel — environment template.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` (already gitignored) and fill in real values there.
# NEVER put a real value in this file — it is tracked in git.
#
# Before deploying anywhere, run:
#   .venv/bin/python scripts/preflight_secrets.py
# It verifies every REQUIRED var below is set, that the trading key is an
# agent wallet (not the master), that .env.local is gitignored/untracked/0600,
# and that no secret value has leaked into the git index. See docs/SECRETS.md
# for the full inventory, provisioning steps per deploy target, and rotation
# procedure for every var here.

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Hyperliquid — REQUIRED. Real-money trading credentials.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Agent/API wallet — the key the bot actually signs orders with. Create this
# in the Hyperliquid UI (More > API) as an agent wallet approved by your
# master account, NOT your main wallet's own key. An agent wallet can trade
# but cannot withdraw; the master key can do both.
HYPERLIQUID_WALLET_ADDRESS=0xAGENT0000000000000000000000000000WALLET
HYPERLIQUID_PRIVATE_KEY=0xFAKEAGENTPRIVATEKEY00000000000000000000000000000000000000

# Master account address — where funds actually live. REQUIRED (not just
# optional): preflight compares this against HYPERLIQUID_WALLET_ADDRESS and
# refuses to start if they match, i.e. if the trading key turns out to be the
# master key instead of an agent wallet. This value is a public address, not
# a secret — safe to set even though it lives in this credentials file.
HYPERLIQUID_MASTER_ADDRESS=0xMASTER00000000000000000000000000ACCOUNT

# Master account PRIVATE key — signs treasury transfers/swaps for
# scripts/treasury.py ONLY (spot<->perp<->HIP-3 moves). This key can
# withdraw funds. Keep it on your laptop; never put it in a Fly/k8s secret
# store alongside the trading key — preflight fails the check if it detects
# a deploy context (FLY_APP_NAME / KUBERNETES_SERVICE_HOST) and this is set.
# Leave unset unless you run scripts/treasury.py locally.
# HYPERLIQUID_MASTER_PRIVATE_KEY=0xFAKEMASTERPRIVATEKEY0000000000000000000000000000000000

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Operator console — REQUIRED. Gates every write endpoint on the dashboard.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 16
# Missing = the operator surface 503s closed (safe default, but you lose
# remote control of the bot) — preflight still treats this as required for a
# real deploy.
PATHIEL_OPERATOR_TOKEN=fake0000000000000000000000000000

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# LLM — there is no API key. The desk thesis writer (services/thesis) goes
# through services/llm, the local Claude Code CLI; `claude` must be on PATH
# and signed in. PATHIEL_LLM_MODEL pins the model (default: probed once).
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# PATHIEL_LLM_MODEL=claude-opus-4-8

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Alt-data — OPTIONAL. Every one of these degrades gracefully to "no data"
# when absent; nothing here blocks the bot from starting or trading.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Desk intel hard data (services/intel/sources). Each source is skipped,
# and the desk brief's `stale` list says so, when its key is missing.
#   EIA_API_KEY      — US crude/gas inventories and storage (https://www.eia.gov/opendata/)
#   FRED_API_KEY     — rates, dollar, inflation series (https://fred.stlouisfed.org/docs/api/api_key.html)
#   CONGRESS_API_KEY — bills and hearings for the policy watch (https://api.congress.gov/sign-up/)
# EIA_API_KEY=fakeEIA000000000000000000000000000000000
# FRED_API_KEY=fakefred00000000000000000000000000
# CONGRESS_API_KEY=fakeCongress0000000000000000000000000000



# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
